@*
    The one place a cover photograph is rendered. Replaces the inline
    style="background-image:url('@x')" that was repeated at ten call sites.

    Three reasons it is a real <img> and not a background:

    1. A background image cannot carry alt text, cannot be lazy-loaded, cannot declare its own
       dimensions, and cannot offer a srcset. All four of those are free here.
    2. width/height are set from the aspect ratio so the browser reserves the box before the bytes
       arrive. Without that, every late-loading photo shifts the page under the reader — and it
       would also invalidate any scroll-linked animation's trigger positions.
    3. Security. `style="background-image:url('@x')"` HTML-encodes the value, but the browser
       HTML-*decodes* before the CSS parser runs, so a quote in an admin-authored URL round-trips
       and can break out of url() into arbitrary CSS declarations. There is no CSP on this site yet,
       which makes that a stored CSS-injection primitive. <img src="@x"> has no equivalent escape.

    ALT TEXT. Pass Alt: null for a decorative cover — one sitting directly above the heading that
    already names it. That is the common case and it is correct: a screen reader announcing the same
    phrase twice is worse than silence. Pass real Alt only when the image carries information the
    surrounding text does not (gallery photographs, for instance, where ExperienceImage.AltText
    exists precisely for this). Never auto-fill Alt from a title.

    Model: (string? Url, string? Alt, string Ratio, string Sizes, bool Eager)
*@
@model VIHouse.WebUI.ViewModels.Shared.CoverImageViewModel

<div class="cover cover--@Model.Ratio">
    @if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.Url))
    {
        @* No image set. A crest on the brand green reads as a deliberate placeholder rather than a
           broken box, which matters because covers are admin-entered and will often be empty. *@
        <div class="cover__fallback" aria-hidden="true">
            <partial name="_Crest" />
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        <img class="cover__img"
             src="@Model.Src"
             srcset="@Model.SrcSet"
             sizes="@Model.Sizes"
             alt="@(Model.Alt ?? string.Empty)"
             width="@Model.Width"
             height="@Model.Height"
             loading="@(Model.Eager ? "eager" : "lazy")"
             decoding="async"
             @(Model.Eager ? "fetchpriority=high" : "") />
    }
</div>
